{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/483560-the-most-game-breaking-moment-you-had-in-your-tables","id":483560,"title":"the most game breaking moment you had in your tables","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-17T08:38:49-07:00","id":483560,"title":"the most game breaking moment you had in your tables","content":"i was running a game of Hunter The Reckoning...and i had 2 imbueds that ended up as Waywards....Holy shit did it derailed fast","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T09:44:43-07:00","id":483672,"title":"","content":"<br /> Not campaign destroying stuff, but super-regeneration fueled by GM brain farts is pretty game breaking.<br /> <br /> I got tired one night during a combat challenge and completely blanked on how Garou regeneration rules worked. Our pack's Shadow Lord Ragabash was dead set on fighting the scion of the local Get of Fenris elder for whatever reason and he finally ended up needling her into a duel. The two squared off and out came the claws, but yours truly allowed for not only regeneration rolls without actions, but also to work at difficulty 6.<br /> <br /> And restore a number of health levels equal to successes.<br /> <br /> AND WORK ON AGGRO DAMAGE.<br /> <br /> I have no idea what I was thinking, but what followed was the silliest slapfight ever had in my WtA game. The Fenrir princess tore our New Moon a series of new holes, but thanks to my ridiculous bungle he not only survived half a dozen attacks raining down, he even got in a few solid licks of his own, thanks to the vagaries of the dice. The packs looked on in disbelief as the proud Ahroun beat the asthmatic Garou only to see his wounds heal nigh-instantaneously and the fight dragged on and on and on. Only when the Ragabash rolled truly abysmally for a couple turns in a row did combat mercifully end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 04-17-2015, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T10:49:29-07:00","id":488476,"title":"","content":"I once played a True Brujah that punched a psuedo-Antediluvian to death. Did like 20+ actions and did over 200 levels of damage all in one turn. GM turned to me and said I broke through his plot armor and killed him after ripping out his heart. This was a Dark Ages game were Vampires had auto damage from Potence and I spent like my entire 40 points of blood in one turn thanks to being able to cheese through my Gen cap. Was hilarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T12:59:31-07:00","id":488619,"title":"","content":"Not game-breaking in the sense of twisting the rules, but if we're talking about going counter to the mood: in one of my first few games playing back in the 90s, several of my group got into a firefight with a thug who revealed himself to be a werewolf. My Wednesday Addams-ish Tremere lowered her generation and burned a boatload of blood points to boost Physical Attributes, but I failed to take into account the increased risk of frenzy due to near-empty pool and promptly lost control of my character. Cue the gun-toting pimp character of the group shouting &quot;UNHAND THAT POOR DEFENSELESS CHILD!&quot; while the werewolf freaked out and found it could neither dislodge nor effectively claw a gradeschool-sized figure attached to its spine like a barnacle. I don't remember if we took it down with bullets or blood loss, but it was the most undignified fight I ever had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T06:00:02-07:00","id":493514,"title":"","content":"First time someone activated Celerity.<br /> <br /> First time someone activated Protean 2 and Celerity.<br /> <br /> Lead to: &quot;But you can't kill <i>him</i>!&quot; Apparently we can.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1916-vertical8","name":"Vertical8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T21:17:57-07:00","id":499767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/483560-the-most-game-breaking-moment-you-had-in-your-tables?p=488476#post488476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once played a True Brujah that punched a psuedo-Antediluvian to death. Did like 20+ actions and did over 200 levels of damage all in one turn. GM turned to me and said I broke through his plot armor and killed him after ripping out his heart. This was a Dark Ages game were Vampires had auto damage from Potence and<b> I spent like my entire 40 points of blood in one turn thanks to being able to cheese through my Gen cap.</b> Was hilarious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure I understand that one... could you elaborate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T07:58:03-07:00","id":506784,"title":"","content":"Mage: the Awakening<br /> <br /> We created editing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T14:57:40-07:00","id":507248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/483560-the-most-game-breaking-moment-you-had-in-your-tables?p=506784#post506784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage: the Awakening<br /> <br /> We created editing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T23:39:42-07:00","id":507746,"title":"","content":"Any game: Player says: &quot;I wanna do XYZ.&quot;<br /> Storyteller answers: &quot;Nope. You can't do that.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't talk about someone who obviously wanted to break the rules of the game or who wanted to do something physically impossible.<br /> <br /> Its that moment the storyteller realises you want to solve a scene in a different way than he expected/ prepared for.<br /> <br /> If I want a predefined story, i read a book. And if I want to choose between a number of predefined story-outcomes I play a computer-game.<br /> <br /> so the most game breaking thing I encountered several times is such a &quot;no. You can't do that.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T18:20:05-07:00","id":510294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/483560-the-most-game-breaking-moment-you-had-in-your-tables?p=507248#post507248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you elaborate?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a vulgar Time spell we created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T23:26:45-07:00","id":510463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/483560-the-most-game-breaking-moment-you-had-in-your-tables?p=510294#post510294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a vulgar Time spell we created.</div> </div> </div> </div>One incomplete sentence hardly counts as 'elaborating.'<br /> <br /> If someone 'breaks' a game of Mage, can anyone even tell? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T04:19:41-07:00","id":510533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/483560-the-most-game-breaking-moment-you-had-in-your-tables?p=510463#post510463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone 'breaks' a game of Mage, can anyone even tell? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. If you break a game of another System players stop to have fun and it may be discontinued.<br /> <br /> if you actually manage to break a game of mage you probably broke the space-time-continuum as well and opened a door of ingame paradox to find its way back into our reality.<br /> <br /> seriousl. Dont't break Mage. Don't!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T11:12:46-07:00","id":510897,"title":"","content":"... I was running a campaing of mage (IN SPACE) where a Etherite was fighting a Nephandi in a lovecraftian horror of a ship.<br /> The ship was plumming down onto malfeas and the nephandi managed to escape.<br /> The player notice that she ship is actually Alive....<br /> player sees character sheet while in panic, then he smiles.<br /> Nelson: &quot;I Seduce The Ship.&quot;<br /> me: .......What?<br /> nelson rolls and uses mind to get more successes..<br /> .......He seduces the ship to reduce the speed and allowing him to escape.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> He...Seduced..A Nephandi Lovecraftian Horror Ship....<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T13:51:02-07:00","id":511109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/483560-the-most-game-breaking-moment-you-had-in-your-tables?p=510897#post510897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I was running a campaing of mage (IN SPACE) where a Etherite was fighting a Nephandi in a lovecraftian horror of a ship.<br /> The ship was plumming down onto malfeas and the nephandi managed to escape.<br /> The player notice that she ship is actually Alive....<br /> player sees character sheet while in panic, then he smiles.<br /> Nelson: &quot;I Seduce The Ship.&quot;<br /> me: .......What?<br /> nelson rolls and uses mind to get more successes..<br /> .......He seduces the ship to reduce the speed and allowing him to escape.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> He...Seduced..A Nephandi Lovecraftian Horror Ship....<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That should have ended very very very badly for him. Staring with loving carresses from barbed tentacles dripping with neurotoxin invading him bodily bad then moving on to things getting really interesting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T15:09:02-07:00","id":511199,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think I'd choose dying in the impact rather than the logical conclusion of having a Lovercraftean horror go sweet on me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T09:25:15-07:00","id":518180,"title":"","content":"The most game breaking cWoD moment for my group would probably be the time Saulot failed a soak roll and took unbagodably levels of aggravated damage from a blood-pumped 6th gen Tzimisce with all kinds of weird damage adding stuffs. The expression on the ST's face when he saw his own roll was priceless. The expression on the Tzimisce player's face was likewise priceless, made even moreso when she said in a sheepish voice &quot;I'm really super sorry I killed Saulot...&quot;<br /> <br /> We all agreed right after that it absolutely MUST have been someone impersonating Saulot who died, because Saulot couldn't REALLY be one-shotted like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T05:46:04-07:00","id":521693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/483560-the-most-game-breaking-moment-you-had-in-your-tables?p=518180#post518180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most game breaking cWoD moment for my group would probably be the time Saulot failed a soak roll and took unbagodably levels of aggravated damage from a blood-pumped 6th gen Tzimisce with all kinds of weird damage adding stuffs. The expression on the ST's face when he saw his own roll was priceless. The expression on the Tzimisce player's face was likewise priceless, made even moreso when she said in a sheepish voice &quot;I'm really super sorry I killed Saulot...&quot;<br /> <br /> We all agreed right after that it absolutely MUST have been someone impersonating Saulot who died, because Saulot couldn't REALLY be one-shotted like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm constantly amazed that people are constantly amazed by the concept of &quot;if you stat it, they will kill it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T16:56:19-07:00","id":523788,"title":"","content":"In a Mage game back about 13 years ago, in the first session, our group was at the airport in Washington D.C. when the ST pointed out that we could see Vice President Dick Cheney getting off of an airplane and talking to reporters and news cameras. Immediately, one of the players blurts out &quot;I change all the blood in his body to steam&quot;. Almost al the players and the ST got a good laugh out of it and thought it was a great idea. The ST had the player roll to see if he could do it, didn't even ask how he was doing it. It worked and the V.P. exploded. They all laughed and gave each others high-fives. The ST then started to go on with the story with nothing happening with what had just happened. I asked, &quot; shouldn't there be some paradox from that?&quot; The ST looked at me with a look of &quot; why are you ruining a good thing&quot;, but the told the player to take a point of paradox. Just one point. Needless to say, this was how the game was run and how the other players played their characters. None of the rules really mattered. Fortunately, the game only lasted 2 sessions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T17:06:15-07:00","id":523789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/483560-the-most-game-breaking-moment-you-had-in-your-tables?p=523788#post523788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (...) The ST had the player roll to see if he could do it, didn't even ask how he was doing it. It worked and the V.P. exploded. They all laughed and gave each others high-fives. The ST then started to go on with the story with nothing happening with what had just happened. I asked, &quot; shouldn't there be some paradox from that?&quot; The ST looked at me with a look of &quot; why are you ruining a good thing&quot;, but the told the player to take a point of paradox. Just one point. (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in fairness, if the ST was running with something akin to 2nd Ed., then a non-botched vulgar spell *would* only garner a point of automatic Paradox. (And even if using Revised, he'd have gotten presumably 4 -- Prime:2/Forces:3, vulgar, equals 3+1 auto Paradox barring botching -- which, if he didn't have any outstanding Paradox, would fire off and not be *too* much more than annoying/inconvenient.) Still, though, it sounds like they were in it for shits-'n-giggles, which is fine but generally not the tone WoD -- of any edition -- is usually aiming for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T17:49:28-07:00","id":523818,"title":"","content":"It was in front of witnesses, which grants more paradox than just a typical botch, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5540-drakilian","name":"Drakilian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T21:11:57-07:00","id":523964,"title":"","content":"To be honest, it was broadcast live around the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T16:58:10-07:00","id":530408,"title":"","content":"My players' finest game breaking moment was as a pack of Garou who had just gone through their Rite of Passage. They'd been tasked to guard the rear as a more experienced pack attacked a major NPC, who was planned to escape in a helicopter (so the pack could go after her personally later). Nobody had firearms, but I did let them get ahold of a couple of claymore mines since there were going to be a lot of nasties.<br /> <br /> As the NPC's helicopter took off, one of the players picked up a claymore and threw it right into the blades from a very long distance, thanks to high strength and a great roll. Blew the whole thing up. Oops.<br /> <br /> Points for creativity, and a reminder to never, ever put your NPCs in a helicopter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}